<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 4.3 Theoretical intuitions ‣ 4 Proposed Method ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_manualpropositioninner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition </span><a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 4.3 Theoretical intuitions ‣ 4 Proposed Method ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span><span id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The InfoNCE loss in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.3 Information Noise-Contrastive Estimation (InfoNCE) ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\;\geq\;-I(Z;Z_{\mathrm{pos}})+I(Z;Z_{\mathrm{neg}})+\log(B-1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">InfoNCE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>neg</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\;\geq\;-I(Z;Z_{\mathrm{pos}})+I(Z;Z_{\mathrm{neg}})+\log(B-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the batch size, and <math id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;Y)</annotation></semantics></math> is the mutual information between random variables <math id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmmanualpropositioninner1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;Y)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{p(X,Y)}\!\left[\log\frac{p(X,Y)}{p(X)p(Y)}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{p(X,Y)}\!\left[\log\frac{p(X\mid Y)}{p(X)}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;Y)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{p(X,Y)}\!\left[\log\frac{p(X,Y)}{p(X)p(Y)}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{p(X,Y)}\!\left[\log\frac{p(X\mid Y)}{p(X)}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">In general, we can formulate the infoNCE loss as Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}=-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}},\mathbf{z}_{\text{neg}})}\left[\log\frac{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}})}{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}})+\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{\text{neg}})}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mtext>neg</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}=-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}},\mathbf{z}_{\text{neg}})}\left[\log\frac{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}})}{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}})+\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{\text{neg}})}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us simply notate <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\text{pos}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\text{neg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\text{neg}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
This can be split into two terms:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}=-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\left\{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})+\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right\}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}=-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\left\{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})+\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right\}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can easily assume that <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> by leveraging an exponential function in convention. Then, Eq. (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>)  has a lower bound by omitting the positive pair similarity from second term:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\geq-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\geq-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">van den Oord et al. (2019)</a></cite>, function <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> estimates the probability density ratio <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z^{\prime}})}{p(\mathbf{z})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>|</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z^{\prime}})}{p(\mathbf{z})}</annotation></semantics></math> related to mutual information maximization. This formulation of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> induces the following Eq. (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}_{p})}{p(\mathbf{z})}\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})}{p(\mathbf{z})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}_{p})}{p(\mathbf{z})}\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})}{p(\mathbf{z})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-I(Z;Z_{p})+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-I(Z;Z_{p})+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})}\right]-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the property of logarithm and Jensen’s Inequality, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-I(Z;Z_{p})+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})}{B-1}\right]+\log(B-1)-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-I(Z;Z_{p})+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\frac{p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})}{B-1}\right]+\log(B-1)-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-I(Z;Z_{p})+\frac{1}{B-1}\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]+\log(B-1)-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-I(Z;Z_{p})+\frac{1}{B-1}\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]+\log(B-1)-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that negative sample <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>s are sampled in same distribution. According to Law of large numbers, we can approximate <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{B-1}\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]\approx\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}_{n})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{B-1}\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]\approx\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}_{n})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the last inequality Eq. (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) holds.</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{InfoNCE}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-I(Z;Z_{p})+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}_{n})\right]+\log(B-1)-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-I(Z;Z_{p})+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z}~|~\mathbf{z}_{n})\right]+\log(B-1)-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z})}\left[\log p(\mathbf{z})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-I(Z;Z_{p})+I(Z;Z_{n})+\log(B-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-I(Z;Z_{p})+I(Z;Z_{n})+\log(B-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 4.3 Theoretical intuitions ‣ 4 Proposed Method ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmmanualpropositioninner2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_manualpropositioninner">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmmanualpropositioninner2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition </span><a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 4.3 Theoretical intuitions ‣ 4 Proposed Method ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span><span id="Thmmanualpropositioninner2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmmanualpropositioninner2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmmanualpropositioninner2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmmanualpropositioninner2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the loss function defined in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2 Gamma effect: regulated attraction for stable image diversification ‣ 4 Proposed Method ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), the following inequality holds:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L^{\gamma}_{\text{InfoNCE}}}\geq-{\frac{1}{\gamma}}I(Z;Z_{\text{pos}})+I(Z;Z_{\text{neg}})+log(B-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">InfoNCE</mtext><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pos</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">neg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L^{\gamma}_{\text{InfoNCE}}}\geq-{\frac{1}{\gamma}}I(Z;Z_{\text{pos}})+I(Z;Z_{\text{neg}})+log(B-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Compared to Equation Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), similarity function <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z,z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z,z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}(z,z^{\prime})=\text{exp}(\frac{sim(z,z^{\prime})}{\gamma})=\{f(z,z^{\prime})\}^{\frac{1}{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>exp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}(z,z^{\prime})=\text{exp}(\frac{sim(z,z^{\prime})}{\gamma})=\{f(z,z^{\prime})\}^{\frac{1}{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, Equation Eq. (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) can be rewritten as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{\gamma}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\geq-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log\{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\}^{1\over\gamma}\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{\gamma}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\geq-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log\{f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\}^{1\over\gamma}\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-{1\over\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-{1\over\gamma}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})}\left[\log f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{p})\right]+\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}_{n})}\left[\log\sum^{B-1}_{i=1}f(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{(i)}_{n})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following similar derivations with Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we can simply show that <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\gamma}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\geq-\frac{1}{\gamma}I(Z;Z_{p})+I(Z;Z_{n})+\log(B-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>InfoNCE</mtext><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\gamma}_{\text{InfoNCE}}\geq-\frac{1}{\gamma}I(Z;Z_{p})+I(Z;Z_{n})+\log(B-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Pseudocode</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Detailed algorithm for our sampling method is provided in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix D Use of Large Language Models ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Evaluation metrics</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image Quality and Prompt Alignment:</span> To measure the quality and textual relevance of the generated images, we employ a suite of widely-recognized automated metrics.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLIPScore:</span> This metric evaluates the semantic consistency between a generated image and its corresponding text prompt by calculating the cosine similarity of their embeddings from a pre-trained CLIP model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hessel et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PickScore:</span> We use PickScore <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirstain et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, a reward model trained on large-scale human preferences, to assess the overall aesthetic quality and prompt alignment of the images.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image-Reward:</span> As a complementary metric, Image-Reward <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2023</a>)</cite> is another human-preference-based reward model that provides scores reflecting the general quality of the generated content.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diversity:</span> To evaluate the intra-prompt diversity of the generated images, we utilize two distinct metrics that capture different aspects of variation.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vendi Score:</span> The Vendi Score <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Friedman &amp; Dieng, 2023</a>)</cite> measures the diversity of a set of samples by analyzing the eigenvalue distribution of their similarity matrix. It provides a holistic assessment of both the variety and balance of the generated images.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mean Pairwise Similarity (MSS):</span> This metric directly quantifies the average similarity between all unique pairs of images generated for a single prompt. We first extract image features using the self-supervised descriptor for image copy detection (SSCD) model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pizzi et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. Then, we compute the pairwise cosine similarity matrix of these features and calculate the mean of its off-diagonal elements. A lower MSS value indicates higher diversity, as images in the set are, on average, less similar to one another.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Hyperparameter settings</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For our main experiments, we use a set of 2K prompts, with each prompt generating a batch of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> images. The number of inference steps was set to 50 for Stable Diffusion 1.5 and XL, and 28 for Stable Diffusion 3. The batch size (<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>) was set to 5 for SD1.5 and SD3, and 3 for SDXL. The specific hyperparameters for our proposed method are detailed in Table <a href="#A2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ B.3 Hyperparameter settings ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Diverse Text-to-Image Generation via Contrastive Noise Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. As shown in the table, most settings are shared across different T2I backbones, highlighting the robustness of our approach to hyperparameter choices.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Model-specific hyperparameters for our proposed method.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter</span></th>
<td id="A2.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stable Diffusion 1.5</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stable Diffusion XL</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stable Diffusion 3</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">CFG Scale</th>
<td id="A2.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">6.0</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">6.0</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">7.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Optimization Steps (<math id="A2.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{opt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{opt}</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A2.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Gamma (<math id="A2.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A2.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.0</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.0</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Window Size (<math id="A2.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A2.T2.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">16</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">16</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">32</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Learning Rate (<math id="A2.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A2.T2.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.01</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.01</td>
<td id="A2.T2.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.001</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Analyses and Results</h2>

<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:39%;"><img src="2510.03813v1/figures/plots/impact_gamma.png" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:220/173;" width="220" height="173" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Impact of <math id="A3.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. The Pareto frontier of PickScore vs. Vendi Score.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Gamma Effect: Stabilizing optimization process</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the stability of our proposed method, we conduct an ablation study on the hyperparameter <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to analyze its impact on output variability. We set <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to values of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1.0,0.9,0.8,0.7\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1.0,0.9,0.8,0.7\}</annotation></semantics></math>. To ensure that our findings are not contingent on a specific learning rate, we vary the learning rate <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> within the range of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.01,0.02]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.02</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.01,0.02]</annotation></semantics></math>. For each setting of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate 5 images per prompt, collecting a total of 5K images using SD1.5 model. We then compute evaluation metrics and calculate their sample variance to quantify the statistical variability of the outputs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T3" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:42%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span><span id="A3.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gamma Effect.</span> Subscripts <math id="A3.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="VS,CS,PS,IR" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">VS,CS,PS,IR</annotation></semantics></math> mean Vendi Score, CLIPScore, PickScore, Image-Reward, respectively.</figcaption>
